      "blind": {
        "done": [
          "Patch file (tools/artifacts/tigervnc/tigervnc-dib-clipboard.patch) touches exactly the requested files: common/rfb/SConnection.cxx/h, VNCSConnectionST, VNCServer(ST), and unix/xserver/hw/vnc/{XserverDesktop.cc/h, vncExtInit.cc/h, vncSelection.c/h}, adding a parallel image/DIB call chain alongside the existing text path",
          "tools/mkimage.sh installs the committed patched .deb (tigervnc-standalone-server/tigervnc-common +codoceh2) via dpkg -i + apt-get install -f instead of stock apt, and asserts the installed dpkg version carries +codoceh2 (step_content_checks)",
          "The .deb's Xtigervnc binary and the one actually unpacked from the current build/image/rootfs.tar.zst (built 2026-08-28, matching the latest commit) both contain the patched clipboard-image symbols (12 occurrences of *ClipboardImageData*), confirming the pipeline artifact is genuinely the patched build, not stock upstream",
          "Live-booted the real patched Xtigervnc from the built rootfs in a chroot and confirmed via raw RFB protocol handshake that Extended Clipboard Caps now advertises the DIB format bit (flags=0x1f000009), fixing the exact defect the project's own pre-patch diagnosis (commit bae3340) documented as missing (0x1f000001, text-only)",
          "Plain text clipboard continues to work correctly through the patched server with Extended Clipboard negotiated (classic ServerCutText round-trip verified live) -- no regression",
          "The X11 glue layer (vncSelection.c) correctly recognizes image/bmp as a clipboard target, adds it to TARGETS, detects ownership changes, and routes ConvertSelection/property-notify handling to the new image-specific code paths, confirmed via live debug log lines matching the patch's own LOG_DEBUG strings",
          "Android client-side unit tests for the DIB codec and RFB Extended Clipboard client code pass (DibCodecTest: 4/4, ScreenRfbClientTest: 31/31, 0 failures)"
        ],
        "missing": [
          "Could not perform the specifically requested live verification method (SSH+xclip on the desktop + the CodocehStol Android app) -- no Android device is reachable via adb in this environment (adb devices returns empty)",
          "Full end-to-end DIB delivery over the wire (Notify -> Request -> Provide completing in either direction) did not complete in repeated live protocol tests against the real patched server, despite the handshake and X11-side selection handling executing correctly up to that point -- could not determine whether this is a genuine gap in the patch (e.g. requestClipboard() possibly still only requesting UTF8, a function not included in the given diff) or an artifact of a hand-rolled test client not matching real client sequencing",
          "No evidence in git history of a live re-verification with the actual patched server after it was built into the .deb -- the only live-testing commit (bae3340) predates the patch and documents the server NOT supporting DIB; the two subsequent commits (f0a18a1, d11e474) are build-pipeline-robustness fixes only, not a re-run of the live E2E test",
          "tools/checkimage.sh, the project's own separate image-acceptance checker, has no awareness of the TigerVNC patch/version at all -- verification exists only inside mkimage.sh's own build-time step",
          "All tigervnc-dib-clipboard work (including the pipeline-embedding commits) lives only on branch feature/screen-zoom and has not been merged into main"
